    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate leaning heavily on **Yordan Alvarez** (85.83) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (79.70) as the foundation of our offensive strategy. **Yordan Alvarez** remains our premier play, boasting an elite 0.423 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against Miller, who carries a shaky 4.68 xERA. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our highest-upside play for stealing bases; facing Ritchie\u2014whose 5.68 xERA is the softest on the board\u2014positions **Pete Crow-Armstrong** to capitalize on his elite sprint speed and aggressive base-running environment. We are also monitoring the wind conditions for **Kyle Schwarber** (62.66), whose lead-off spot and favorable wind-out factors provide a solid floor despite facing a tougher arm in Gray.\n\nStrategic platoon and lineup advantages are also boosting several mid-tier starts. **Luke Raley** (62.37) benefits from a significant SP skill edge and his ability to run against a slow-delivery opponent, making him a prime target for a multi-category contribution. While we are keeping a close watch on **Hyeseong Kim** (43.20) and **Casey Schmitt** (44.36) given their reliance on assumed lineup slots, both remain in the active group to ensure our game caps are utilized efficiently against their respective left-handed matchups. The most difficult decision this morning involved **Carson Benge** (42.46), who narrowly missed the starting cut; while his leadoff order provided a nice boost, his historical platoon disadvantage against Valdez proved too heavy a tax compared to the efficiency scores generated by our locked-in outfielders and middle infielders.\n\nInvestors should note that we are currently navigating a thin bench, with **Trea Turner** and **Christian Yelich** unavailable due to rest and **Lars Nootbaar** remaining on the IL. We are operating without high-end safety nets, placing extra pressure on **Junior Caminero** (60.28) and **Caleb Durbin** (57.80) to maintain production against their respective right-handed opponents. While **Dillon Dingler** (40.79) sits near our minimum threshold, his role in a favorable order spot keeps him in the mix. We continue to monitor **Gary Sanchez**, **Josh Smith**, **Zac Veen**, **Pedro Ramirez**, and **Luis Pena** on the roster periphery for potential late-game shifts if official lineups drift from our current assumptions.",
